From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:55:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] LumaUI Settings: Mobile Network while a modem is present

Settings' LumaUI window lists its destinations from a fixed table, and
the wwan panel was in none of them, so a phone with a modem had no way
to its mobile data, APN, roaming or SIM settings.

A live adapter watches ModemManager's objects on the system bus (never
starting it) and reports "modem" while one has a capability the wwan
panel supports, as cc_wwan_panel_static_init_func decides. Mobile
Network (radio-tower) is listed after Wi-Fi only then; the sidebar
follows a modem coming or going. The page is the wwan panel; NMClient
and MMManager, which GNOME's window puts in the object storage at
startup, are added before the panel opens, which also makes the "wwan"
deep link work. Without a modem nothing changes. Test:
luma-settings-live-modem against a stand-in ModemManager.
